    {
      "datasource": {
        "uid": "$ds_prometheus"
      },
      "description": "How long writes were blocked by compaction, per member. Every 5 minutes compaction deletes old revisions in batches of 1000: a batch reads them from the database file, deletes them and commits. Writes wait, reads do not.\n\nA spike on 'RPC Duration p99 by Node' of about the same height at the same time: the spike is compaction.\n\nBars of seconds with a spike on 'DB Reads from Disk' at the same time: the old revisions are read from disk, the database is not in the page cache, see 'DB in Page Cache'.\n\nBars of seconds without reads from disk: the batch writes a lot, the database is large or fragmented, see 'DB Size', defrag helps.\n\n'4 s+' is the ceiling of the metric, the real pause was longer, the axis stops there. 'Disk Sync Duration p99' does not show these pauses: one slow commit among thousands is outside p99.",
      "fieldConfig": {
        "defaults": {
          "color": {
            "mode": "palette-classic"
          },
          "custom": {
            "axisBorderShow": false,
            "axisCenteredZero": false,
            "axisColorMode": "text",
            "axisLabel": "",
            "axisPlacement": "auto",
            "axisSoftMax": 0,
